    return 1
  fi

  # 24b. #733 duplicate control: the row IDENTITY is the UNIT, never
  #      (unit, pr, issue). A re-record carrying a DIFFERENT triple -- here the
  #      second call changes --pr and omits --issue -- must still UPDATE that
  #      unit's row. The old key invented a SECOND identity the consumer never
  #      had, so this shape landed on a new key and APPENDED a duplicate that
  #      purge refuses to remove (#707), making it permanent; a live unit
  #      carried two rows when #733 was found. Case 24 re-records the SAME
